sections.theory:
b. public access specifier

public members are accessible from anywhere where the object is visible i.e. within the class, in the derived classes and in the main function.

Consider the following program to demonstrate the visibility of public members of a class.

// public access specifier example 1
#include<iostream.h>
#include<conio.h>
class PublicTest
{
public:
int X=10; // Public data member
void showPublic() // Public member function
{
cout<< “X= "<<X;
}
};
int main()
{
PublicTest PT1; //PT1 is an object of class PublicTest
PT1.X; //access private data members
PT1.showPublic(); // access public member function
getch();
return 0;
}

In the above program, the class PublicTest is defined which comprise of one data member X and one member function showPublic() in its public part. The data member is accessed within the member function showPublic() and outside the class, i.e. in main() function, without generating any error message. Similarly, the member function showPublic() is also accessed in main() function.

If no access specifier is mentioned in a class for a member then it will combined as private by default.

The following program demonstrates private and public access specifier.

#include<iostream.h>
#include<conio.h>
class Access
{
int A; // private by default
void GetA() // private by default
{
cout<<"I am private member accessible only through public member function"<<endl;
}
public:
int B; // public
void GetB()
{
GetA();
cout<<"I am B in public"<<endl;
}
};
int main()
{
Access cAccess; //cAccess is an object of the class Access
//cAccess.A = 2; // WRONG because A is private data member
//cAccess.GetA(); //WRONG because GetA() is private member function
cAccess.B=10; // Okay because B is public data member
cAccess.GetB(); // Okay because GetB() is public member function
getch();
return 0;
}

The above program explains the scope (or accessibility) of the private and public data members and member functions in detail. Also, comments are added with each line of code in main() program for the explanation of its accessibility level.

The output of the program is:

I am private member accessible only through public member function
I am B in public

sections.urdu:
b. public ایکسس اسپیسیفائر

public اراکین ہر اس جگہ سے قابلِ رسائی ہیں جہاں آبجیکٹ نظر آتا ہو یعنی کلاس کے اندر، ماخوذ کلاسز میں اور main فنکشن میں۔

کلاس کے public اراکین کی نمائش واضح کرنے کے لیے درج ذیل پروگرام پر غور کریں۔

// public access specifier example 1
#include<iostream.h>
#include<conio.h>
class PublicTest
{
public:
int X=10; // Public data member
void showPublic() // Public member function
{
cout<< “X= "<<X;
}
};
int main()
{
PublicTest PT1; //PT1 is an object of class PublicTest
PT1.X; //access private data members
PT1.showPublic(); // access public member function
getch();
return 0;
}

اوپر کے پروگرام میں کلاس PublicTest بیان کی گئی ہے جس کے public حصے میں ایک ڈیٹا ممبر X اور ایک ممبر فنکشن showPublic() ہے۔ ڈیٹا ممبر تک ممبر فنکشن showPublic() کے اندر اور کلاس کے باہر یعنی main() فنکشن میں کسی خرابی کے پیغام کے بغیر رسائی ہوتی ہے۔ اسی طرح ممبر فنکشن showPublic() تک بھی main() فنکشن میں رسائی ہوتی ہے۔

اگر کلاس میں کسی ممبر کے لیے کوئی ایکسس اسپیسیفائر نہ لکھا ہو تو وہ بطورِ طے شدہ private شمار ہوگا۔

درج ذیل پروگرام private اور public ایکسس اسپیسیفائر واضح کرتا ہے۔

#include<iostream.h>
#include<conio.h>
class Access
{
int A; // private by default
void GetA() // private by default
{
cout<<"I am private member accessible only through public member function"<<endl;
}
public:
int B; // public
void GetB()
{
GetA();
cout<<"I am B in public"<<endl;
}
};
int main()
{
Access cAccess; //cAccess is an object of the class Access
//cAccess.A = 2; // WRONG because A is private data member
//cAccess.GetA(); //WRONG because GetA() is private member function
cAccess.B=10; // Okay because B is public data member
cAccess.GetB(); // Okay because GetB() is public member function
getch();
return 0;
}

اوپر کا پروگرام private اور public ڈیٹا ممبرز اور ممبر فنکشنز کا دائرہ (یا رسائی) تفصیل سے واضح کرتا ہے۔ نیز main() پروگرام میں کوڈ کی ہر لائن کے ساتھ اس کی رسائی کی سطح کی وضاحت کے لیے تبصرے شامل کیے گئے ہیں۔

پروگرام کا آؤٹ پٹ یہ ہے:

I am private member accessible only through public member function
I am B in public

